   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Try running the model through <a href=\"https://github.com/kaskr/tmbstan#examples\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/kaskr/tmbstan%23examples&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461698451000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0yaCVtDv4xraEygO527vhJ\">tmbstan</a> and look at the posterior for the slope compared to the MLE and SE. I&#39;d be surprised if it gives you something meaningfully different but I don&#39;t understand the theory of these models well. -Cole</div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Fri, Jul 21, 2023 at 9:40 PM &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tmb-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211);max-width:850px;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n  <div style=\"background-color:rgb(245,245,245);padding:10px 20px\">\r\n    <table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%\">\r\n      <tbody>\r\n        <tr>\r\n          <td style=\"width:70%\">\r\n            <span style=\"font:18px/20px arial;color:rgb(51,51,51)\">\r\n              <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email#!forum/tmb-users/topics\" style=\"text-decoration:none;color:rgb(51,51,51)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail%23!forum/tmb-users/topics&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461698451000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0J3czjkH1KRt0_H_0c6UWa\">\r\n              tmb-...@googlegroups.com</a>\r\n            </span>\r\n          </td>\r\n          <td style=\"text-align:right;width:30%\">\r\n            <span style=\"font:20px/24px arial\"><a style=\"color:rgb(221,75,57);text-decoration:none\" href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email/#!overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail/%23!overview&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461698451000&amp;usg=AOvVaw052SkP_a-gqjaTCKD_gj-Z\">Google Groups</a></span>\r\n          </td>\r\n          <td style=\"width:32px\">\r\n            <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email/#!overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail/%23!overview&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461698451000&amp;usg=AOvVaw052SkP_a-gqjaTCKD_gj-Z\"><img style=\"border:0px;vertical-align:middle\" src=\"https://ci5.googleusercontent.com/proxy/4SGWHe9midrWMDxDIJMQraTMMgnAU71soPZ0D28IOSZcs66TdyRoCqyIhaTt-kwo0YKv2lRo05RkwsGFZdnFhdvy60XdxNlL2U-B=s0-d-e1-ft#http://www.google.com/images/icons/product/groups-32.png\"></a>\r\n          </td>\r\n        </tr>\r\n      </tbody>\r\n    </table>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <div style=\"padding:20px;background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\">\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"font-family:arial;color:rgb(34,34,34);padding:0px\">\r\n  <a name=\"m_3423354479691357793_m_6668638545837119013_digest_top\" style=\"font-size:21px\" rel=\"nofollow\">\r\n  \r\n  \r\n    Topic digest\r\n  \r\n  </a><br>\r\n  <span style=\"font-size:11px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email#!forum/tmb-users/topics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail%23!forum/tmb-users/topics&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461698451000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0J3czjkH1KRt0_H_0c6UWa\">View all topics</a>\r\n  </span>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font:13px/18px arial;color:rgb(34,34,34);padding:0px;margin-bottom:30px\">\r\n  <ul style=\"margin-left:3px;padding-left:0px\">\r\n  \r\n    <li>\r\n      <a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_3423354479691357793_m_6668638545837119013_group_thread_0\" rel=\"nofollow\">\r\n      Digest for tmb-...@googlegroups.com - 1 update in 1 topic</a> -\r\n      <span style=\"color:rgb(119,119,119)\">2 Updates</span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  \r\n    <li>\r\n      <a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_3423354479691357793_m_6668638545837119013_group_thread_1\" rel=\"nofollow\">\r\n      Possible bias when fitting linear regression with errors in variables using TMB</a> -\r\n      <span style=\"color:rgb(119,119,119)\">4 Updates</span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  \r\n  </ul>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <a name=\"m_3423354479691357793_m_6668638545837119013_group_thread_0\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a>\r\n  <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0px 5px\">\r\n  \r\n    <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/tmb-users/t/679ef676ea6dcf99?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/tmb-users/t/679ef676ea6dcf99?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461698451000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1znMU-rGlCbRDodgcvqSHQ\">\r\n      Digest for tmb-...@googlegroups.com - 1 update in 1 topic\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n      <tbody><tr><td style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(46,46,46);font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211)\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:rgb(177,176,176);font-size:15px\">\r\n          Cole Monnahan - NOAA Federal &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">cole.m...@noaa.gov</a>&gt;: Jul 21 09:36AM -0700\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        I don&#39;t see any immediate bugs in the code. I also ran the code with 100<br>\r\ndifferent seeds and your coverage is about 85% for the slope. It appears<br>\r\nslightly positively biased actually. I&#39;m not super familiar with these<br>\r\nmodels. Would you expect a 95% coverage? -Cole<br>\r\n <br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n      <tr><td style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(46,46,46);font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211)\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:rgb(177,176,176);font-size:15px\">\r\n          DM Gillis &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">astros...@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Jul 21 01:19PM -0700\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        That could be it... I just ran it with one seed and hoped that it would be <br>\r\nwell behaved (very naive). I will simulate more and be especially careful <br>\r\nwhen applying it to real data (including examining repeated simulations <br>\r\nwith the fitted model parameters). Thanks for your exploration and all the <br>\r\nbest for the weekend!<br>\r\n <br>\r\nCheers, Darren<br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n  </tbody></table>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_3423354479691357793_m_6668638545837119013_digest_top\" rel=\"nofollow\">Back to top</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <a name=\"m_3423354479691357793_m_6668638545837119013_group_thread_1\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a>\r\n  <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0px 5px\">\r\n  \r\n    <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/tmb-users/t/eceda1fbfa379f65?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/tmb-users/t/eceda1fbfa379f65?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461698451000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3lCwL-gOA3kppT66YVwT0S\">\r\n      Possible bias when fitting linear regression with errors in variables using TMB\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n      <tbody><tr><td style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(46,46,46);font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211)\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:rgb(177,176,176);font-size:15px\">\r\n          Hans Skaug &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hsk...@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Jul 21 12:20AM -0700\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        Hi, I think this is more a statistical theory question than a question <br>\r\nabout TMB. There are different<br>\r\nassumptions that can be made for this model:<br>\r\n<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Errors-in-variables_models#Terminology_and_assumptions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Errors-in-variables_models%23Terminology_and_assumptions&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461698451000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2qVrMG4RiOlKmrDvVy90Br\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Errors-in-variables_models#Terminology_and_assumptions</a><br>\r\n <br>\r\nYour approach seems to add one parameter (del) per observation, which may <br>\r\nbe problematic.<br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n      <tr><td style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(46,46,46);font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211)\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:rgb(177,176,176);font-size:15px\">\r\n          DM Gillis &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">astros...@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Jul 21 05:47AM -0700\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        Thank you for the quick response.  There may be different model assumptions <br>\r\nthat work better, but I am interested in this form:<br>\r\n <br>\r\n<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Errors-in-variables_models#Simple_linear_model\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Errors-in-variables_models%23Simple_linear_model&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461698451000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0-zuru4JX8Al-FMdXwMpiW\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Errors-in-variables_models#Simple_linear_model</a><br>\r\n <br>\r\n <a href=\"https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/72c8882e35c59a196c8115548e47a19b0555360e\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/72c8882e35c59a196c8115548e47a19b0555360e&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461698451000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3EDHF3_zY4QnKU53SCXlNw\">https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/72c8882e35c59a196c8115548e47a19b0555360e</a><br>\r\n <br>\r\nbecause it would be straight forward to extend it to other models besides <br>\r\nlinear regression. However, I am not sure that either 1) this form can be <br>\r\ncoded in TMB, and 2) if I have done it correctly. In this code, both have <br>\r\nrandom components: Y (represented in the classic errors) and X (the del&#39;s) <br>\r\n. If this formulation cannot be executed in TMB then I will seek other <br>\r\nsolutions (JAGS or STAN, perhaps), but I was hoping to stay in the world of <br>\r\nlikelihood (and learn some TMB at the same time).  Thanks again for taking <br>\r\nthe time to review this issue.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nRegards, Darren<br>\r\n <br>\r\nOn Friday, July 21, 2023 at 4:20:26 AM UTC-3 Hans Skaug wrote:<br>\r\n <br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n      <tr><td style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(46,46,46);font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211)\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:rgb(177,176,176);font-size:15px\">\r\n          Mollie Brooks &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mollie...@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Jul 21 06:23PM +0200\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        In response to Han’s comment, I tried running it with del as a random variable and didn’t do any better. I don’t know why, because the Wikipedia article seems to say it should be identifiable in this case.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nObj &lt;- MakeADFun(data=Data, <br>\r\n\tparameters=Params, <br>\r\n\trandom=c(&quot;del&quot;),<br>\r\n\tDLL=model_name,<br>\r\n\tsilent=FALSE)<br>\r\n <br>\r\nMollie<br>\r\n <br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n      <tr><td style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255);color:rgb(46,46,46);font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid rgb(211,211,211)\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:rgb(177,176,176);font-size:15px\">\r\n          DM Gillis &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">astros...@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Jul 21 12:15PM -0700\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        Yes, when I do the same it returns the OLS slope, which makes sense to me <br>\r\nsince setting it to &quot;random&quot; means it will be integrated out and should not <br>\r\nimpact the estimates (just their SEs). However, I want it to have an impact <br>\r\nand move the slope around the true value of 2 :(  Perhaps TMB only works <br>\r\nwith latent random variables/effects and not variation added to predictors <br>\r\nthat are not not LRVs to be integrated out.Thanks for taking the time to <br>\r\ncheck and enjoy the weekend! <br>\r\n <br>\r\nDarren<br>\r\n <br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n  </tbody></table>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_3423354479691357793_m_6668638545837119013_digest_top\" rel=\"nofollow\">Back to top</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  </div>\r\n  <div style=\"background-color:rgb(245,245,245);padding:5px 20px\">\r\n  <table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%\">\r\n  <tbody><tr>\r\n    <td style=\"padding-top:4px;font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(99,99,99);font-size:11px\">\r\n      \r\n      You received this digest because you&#39;re subscribed to updates for this group. You can change your settings on the <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email#!forum/tmb-users/join\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail%23!forum/tmb-users/join&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461698451000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3VcHzBEJrGKZajrgYgbDZx\">group membership page</a>.<br>\r\n      To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">tmb-users+...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr></tbody>\r\n  </table>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</blockquote></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
